# Hoisted, not pnpm's default isolated layout.
#
# Every dev container bind-mounts the whole repo (docker-compose.yml: `.:/app`) and protects
# only ONE path from that mount per service: a named volume at /app/node_modules. pnpm's default
# linker instead creates node_modules *inside each workspace package* (e.g.
# packages/geo-core/node_modules/proj4) so that a real dependency resolves. Those per-package
# node_modules directories live inside the bind-mounted tree and are not covered by any volume,
# so on the host (which has no node_modules anywhere) they simply don't exist at runtime -- any
# dependency that isn't hoisted becomes unresolvable (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND) the moment the owning
# package's code actually runs.
#
# Hoisting puts every dependency in the one root node_modules that IS covered by each service's
# named volume, so this has to stay set for the Docker dev workflow to work at all.
node-linker=hoisted
